From 6bdb42e0db01f3e62449b257edbab22bc912ca93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: brunduk <nikolai.viktorovich@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 10:37:57 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] a/tracking: SLAM_CONFIG_PIPELINE_ONLY, config sweeps without
 hand-writing calibration

SLAM_CONFIG is all-or-nothing: passing a file makes t_slam stop sending the
driver's calibration, on the assumption that the file carries it. That makes
tuning a single pipeline parameter against a real device expensive -- the whole
device calibration has to be re-expressed in the tracker's own format first,
which is both work and a second place for it to be wrong.

SLAM_CONFIG_PIPELINE_ONLY=1 declares that the file carries pipeline settings
only, and keeps sending the driver calibration. Default off, so the existing
meaning of SLAM_CONFIG is unchanged.

Needs the matching change on the tracker side to accept a config file with no
calibration in it (for Basalt: --cam-calib stops being required).

This is what turned the 2026-08-12 Reverb G2 6DoF investigation from reading
code into measuring: each config variant became a one-line change plus a run.
The result was that Basalt's default detection settings (which are also its
EuRoC settings) are too sparse for the G2's fisheye cameras -- with
grid_size 30 / num_points_cell 3 / min_threshold 3 the static drift went from
thousands of metres to 0.72 m at 60 s. See docs/pruebas.jsonl T162.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/xrt/auxiliary/tracking/t_tracker_slam.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/xrt/auxiliary/tracking/t_tracker_slam.cpp b/src/xrt/auxiliary/tracking/t_tracker_slam.cpp
index 77a0641e1..9a256d2f1 100644
--- a/src/xrt/auxiliary/tracking/t_tracker_slam.cpp
+++ b/src/xrt/auxiliary/tracking/t_tracker_slam.cpp
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@ DEBUG_GET_ONCE_NUM_OPTION(slam_openvr_groundtruth_device, "SLAM_OPENVR_GROUNDTRU
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_NUM_OPTION(slam_prediction_type, "SLAM_PREDICTION_TYPE", long(SLAM_PRED_DEAD_RECKONING))
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(slam_write_csvs, "SLAM_WRITE_CSVS", false)
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(slam_features_enable, "SLAM_FEATURES_ENABLE", false)
+DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(slam_config_pipeline_only, "SLAM_CONFIG_PIPELINE_ONLY", false)
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_BOOL_OPTION(euroc_record, "EUROC_RECORD", false)
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_OPTION(euroc_record_path, "EUROC_RECORD_PATH", nullptr)
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_OPTION(slam_csv_path, "SLAM_CSV_PATH", "evaluation/")
@@ -1512,9 +1513,18 @@ t_slam_create(struct xrt_frame_context *xfctx,
 
 	t.base.get_tracked_pose = t_slam_get_tracked_pose;
 
+	// SLAM_CONFIG is normally all-or-nothing: pass a file and the driver's calibration is no
+	// longer sent, so tuning one pipeline parameter means hand-writing the whole device
+	// calibration in the tracker's own format first. SLAM_CONFIG_PIPELINE_ONLY=1 says the file
+	// carries pipeline settings only, and keeps the driver calibration -- which is what makes a
+	// config sweep against real hardware a one-line change per run instead of a project.
+	bool pipeline_only = debug_get_bool_option_slam_config_pipeline_only();
 	if (!config_file) {
 		SLAM_INFO("Using calibration from driver and default pipeline settings");
 		send_calibration(t, *config->slam_calib); // Not null because of `some_calib`
+	} else if (pipeline_only && some_calib) {
+		SLAM_INFO("Using calibration from driver and pipeline settings from the SLAM_CONFIG file");
+		send_calibration(t, *config->slam_calib);
 	} else {
 		SLAM_INFO("Using sensor calibration provided by the SLAM_CONFIG file");
 	}
